# 1. Rotating cube

<div class="code-path">Code: <code>examples/a1-opengl-cube/</code></div>

The objective of this first example is to display a minimal OpenGL program in a slide: a cube that rotates by
itself, written in raw OpenGL 3.3 with GLFW (about 200 lines). There is no control on screen: the slide sets
the speed and the tilt of the cube through the address of its frame. The same source file is compiled for the
desktop and for the web.

Once built, you should obtain the following result (the web build of this example, set by
`?speed=0.2&tilt=25`):

